Hallo Finn,

Yes! Thank you!
mesh$n <- nrow(mesh$loc) solved the problem!

"original"
summary(mesh)

Manifold: R2
CRS/LegacyPROJ4: +proj=utm +zone=33 +ellps=GRS80 +units=m +no_defs
CRS/WKT: (only shown with verbose = TRUE)
Vertices: 14898
Triangles: 18926
Boundary segm.: 13392 (4 groups: 4 1 2 3)
Interior segm.: 0
xlim: 282980.2 497554.3
ylim: 5563149 5726191
zlim: 0 0

with solution:
mesh$n <- nrow(mesh$loc)
summary(mesh)

Manifold: R2
CRS/LegacyPROJ4: +proj=utm +zone=33 +ellps=GRS80 +units=m +no_defs
CRS/WKT: (only shown with verbose = TRUE)
Vertices: 14083
Triangles: 18926
Boundary segm.: 13392 (4 groups: 4 1 2 3)
Interior segm.: 0
xlim: 282980.2 497554.3
ylim: 5563149 5726191
zlim: 0 0

Tested as well:
inla.setOption(fmesher.evolution=1L)
and this worked too.

I also tried it with the current version 0.1.2.9002. It works.

Thank you Finn for your work!

Best regards from Dresden.

Louis

